sentences.text:
A conjoint reading of Order IX Rule 13 CPC and Section 96(2) CPC indicates that the defendant who suffered an ex-parte decree has two remedies:- (i) either to file an application under Order IX Rule 13 CPC to set aside the ex-parte decree to satisfy the court that summons were not duly served or those served, he was prevented by "sufficient cause" from appearing in the court when the suit was called for hearing;
(ii) to file a regular appeal from the original decree to the first appellate court and challenge the ex-parte decree on merits."
